---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import FinalCta from '../components/FinalCta.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Rokko — A new direction for home-service operations"
  description="Rokko is a new product and marketing direction focused on accountable AI operations for home-service companies."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About Rokko"
    title="Built from the distance between knowing and doing."
    deck="Rokko is a new direction focused on helping home-service operators reach a trustworthy next move without giving up the authority that makes the move accountable."
    tone="moss"
  />

  <section class="section origin">
    <div class="container--content origin__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why this direction</p>
        <h2>Most operating problems do not begin with a lack of software.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="deck">They begin when useful context is spread across systems, decisions arrive without a clear owner, and automation removes the moment where judgment should happen.</p>
        <p>Rokko is being built around a different line: assemble the context, prepare the next supported move, and keep the accountable person in control.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper principles">
    <div class="container--content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Operating principles</p>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="numbered-card"><span class="numbered-card__number">01</span><h3>Evidence over theater</h3><p>Claims, demos, and proof should be tied to something the operator can inspect.</p></article>
        <article class="numbered-card"><span class="numbered-card__number">02</span><h3>Authority over opacity</h3><p>Consequential moves should keep their owner and approval state visible.</p></article>
        <article class="numbered-card"><span class="numbered-card__number">03</span><h3>Operations over novelty</h3><p>The product earns its place by reducing real operating friction, not by performing AI theater.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section commitment">
    <div class="container--content commitment__grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The public standard</p><h2>We will say what is verified—and say when it is not.</h2></div>
      <p class="deck">The current site intentionally withholds unapproved pricing, named customer proof, legal text, and broad capability claims. That boundary is part of how Rokko intends to market the product.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FinalCta title="Show us the operating question you keep asking." />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .origin__grid,
  .commitment__grid { display: grid; gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 8rem); align-items: start; }
  .origin h2,
  .commitment h2 { max-width: 12ch; }
  .principles .numbered-card { min-height: 21rem; }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .origin__grid,
    .commitment__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
</style>
